  "solution": "Given:\n\n(24, 3, 10)\n\n(144, 9, 18)\n\n**Logic:** First no. = [Second no. × (Third no. - 2)]\n\n**(24, 3, 10) →**\n\n⇒ [3 × (10 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (3 × 8) = 24\n\n**(144, 9, 18) →**\n\n⇒ [9 × (18 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (9 × 16) = 144\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n1. (54, 9, 4) →\n\n⇒ [9 × (4 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (9 × 2) = 18\n\n2. (156, 8, 19) →\n\n⇒ [8 × (19 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (8 × 17) = 136\n\n3. (72, 8, 9) →\n\n⇒ [8 × (9 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (8 × 7) = 56\n\n**4. (133, 7, 21) →**\n\n⇒ [7 × (21 - 2)]\n\n⇒ (7 × 19) = **133**\n\nHere, **(133, 7, 21)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (4)\".",
